===========================================================================
Scientific Data Sources and Attributions
===========================================================================
Physical constants, atomic weights, atomic radii, X-ray scattering form
factors, and perceptual palettes in `src/xkcd_matchem/data/` and
`src/xkcd_matchem/style/` compile factual values from the following
verified primary sources:

1. CODATA Recommended Values of the Fundamental Physical Constants: 2022
   Mohr, P. J.; Newell, D. B.; Taylor, B. N.; Tiesinga, E. (2025).
   Reviews of Modern Physics, 97(2), 025002.
   DOI: 10.1103/RevModPhys.97.025002
   Primary data table: NIST Standard Reference Database 121
   (https://physics.nist.gov/constants).

2. Standard Atomic Weights of the Elements (IUPAC / CIAAW)
   Prohaska, T.; Irrgeher, J.; Benefield, J.; Bohlke, J. K.; Chesson, L. A.;
   Coplen, T. B.; Ding, T.; Dunn, P. J. H.; Groning, M.; Holden, N. E.;
   Meijer, H. A. J.; Moossen, H.; Possolo, A.; Takahashi, Y.; Vogl, J.;
   Walczyk, T.; Wang, J.; Wieser, M. E.; Yoneda, S.; Zhu, X.-K.; Meija, J.
   (2022). Pure and Applied Chemistry, 94(5), 573-600.
   DOI: 10.1515/pac-2019-0603
   With 2024 CIAAW updates for Gd (157.249), Lu (174.96669), and Zr (91.222)
   from https://ciaaw.org/atomic-weights.htm, and selected radioactive
   nuclide masses from Prohaska et al. (2022) Table 2.

3. Blue Obelisk Data Repository (BODR) - Elements Dataset
   Guha, R.; Howard, M. T.; Hutchison, G. R.; Murray-Rust, P.; Rzepa, H.;
   Steinbeck, C.; Wegner, J.; Willighagen, E. L. (2006).
   Journal of Chemical Information and Modeling, 46(3), 991-998.
   DOI: 10.1021/ci050400b
   Dataset `elements.xml` dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0
   Universal (BODR COPYING).

4. PubChem Periodic Table Cross-Checks
   Kim, S.; Gindulyte, A.; Zhang, J.; Thiessen, P. A.; Bolton, E. E. (2021).
   Chemistry Teacher International, 3(1), 57-65.
   DOI: 10.1515/cti-2020-0006

5. van der Waals Radii
   - Alvarez, S. (2013). "A cartography of the van der Waals territories".
     Dalton Transactions, 42(24), 8617-8636. DOI: 10.1039/c3dt50599e
     (Table 1, Supplementary Table S1, and Section 6 heuristic
     r_vdw = r_cov + 0.90 A for unmeasured actinides/superheavy elements).
   - Mantina, M.; Chamberlin, A. C.; Valero, R.; Cramer, C. J.;
     Truhlar, D. G. (2009). "Consistent van der Waals Radii for the Whole
     Main Group". The Journal of Physical Chemistry A, 113(19), 5806-5812.
     DOI: 10.1021/jp8111556 (Table 12 main-group radii, including Po, At,
     Rn, Fr, Ra).

6. Atomic X-Ray Scattering Form Factors
   Cromer, D. T.; Mann, J. B. (1967, distributed March 11, 1968).
   "X-Ray Scattering Factors Computed from Numerical Hartree-Fock Wave
   Functions". Los Alamos Scientific Laboratory Report LA-3816.
   DOI: 10.2172/4555098 (Table II Gaussian analytical fits, report pp. 66-69,
   for neutral He (Z=2) through Lr/Lw (Z=103); neutral H (Z=1) uses the
   exact analytical spherical 1s form factor (1 + (2*pi*a_0*s)^2)^(-2)).

7. Okabe & Ito Color Universal Design (CUD) Palette
   Okabe, M.; Ito, K. (2002, modified 2008). "Color Universal Design (CUD):
   How to make figures and presentations that are friendly to Colorblind
   people". https://jfly.uni-koeln.de/color/

8. Jmol CPK Element Color Table
   Jmol Development Team; Herraez, A.; Vervelle, N. "Jmol Colors".
   https://jmol.sourceforge.net/jscolors/ (JmolConstants.java rev. 14469,
   with fallback color #FF1493 for elements 110-118 per documentation).
